{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in one small deterministic specification with clear exploration, short forward progress, and obstacle-specific turn recovery. Action states self-loop on path_clear so uncontrollables are processed first without unnecessarily preempting the intended one-shot controllable, while obstacle events still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion using two simple plant automata",
    "Use one compact policy specification with exactly one controllable action per non-terminal state",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward coverage via random_walk and a short move_forward alternation",
    "Route obstacle_front to a dedicated turn recovery, obstacle_left to clockwise recovery, and obstacle_right to counterclockwise recovery",
    "Return to exploration immediately on path_clear after recovery and avoid full_rotate except as an optional last-resort capability in the plant only"
  ],
